Oops.  This was a boner, yes.  Hang on to the makedefs utility created
at compilation time, in addition to dgn_comp and lev_comp.
"makedefs -e" needs to be run from a directory structure similar to
the way NetHack is packaged -- it looks for dungeon.def in ../dat
(relative to the current directory), and it will not work otherwise.

